From: finalpantasy <finalpantasy@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 10:06:32 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 14/34] D3D11: interpolated frames between recorded frames,
 paced by a presenter thread

FFXII_D3D_INTERP=1 (with FFXII_D3D_RECORD=1) records every frame on a second
deferred context too, with constant-buffer uploads blended halfway between the
previous and current frame (FFXII_D3D_INTERP_T sets the point). A presenter
thread shows the blended frame when the game presents and the real frame half
a measured frame interval later (FFXII_D3D_PACE=0 shows both at once).

- Buffer maps on the main recording context are mirrored by a twin map on the
  blend context with the same data.
- A deferred context sees a dynamic buffer only after a DISCARD map in the
  same command list, so buffers the frame did not write are written into each
  blend list up front from their last contents. Without this, buffers written
  once (fullscreen quads, menu text) drew nothing and blended frames showed
  only the cursor.
- Flush on a recording context is a no-op, and GetData on a query not ended
  in the list being recorded answers from the immediate context, so frames
  no longer break blending (1 Flush and 2 GetData per frame before).
- Immediate-context use is serialized with the presenter by a recursive lock.
- FFXII_D3D_DEBUG=1 enables the D3D11 debug layer and prints its messages.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
